 "| PROVED (defect term with the constant 0.0485883; Proposition W; Lemma LR; Proposition TL; each re-derived by the referee); RELATIVE to Statement O (direction (c)); MEASURED (float64, symmetrised model; no certificate); ARGUED (Phi_1 lower bound); one referee pass (E1 to E5, no verdict change), independent second pass owed (`c18-referee-r17-independent-sources`) "
 "| target: the inequality at defect 0. Proposition W (T-NR in symmetric form with q -> 1; a Beurling-type member) passes the functional equation, the pole clause, N >= 0 and frequencies within delta, and fails only the support clause. ZQ, SG, NR-q and T-NR are excluded through integrality, not through multiplicativity; NR-q is multiplicative on its semigroup. Sign-twisted primes and unimodular twists are members of direction (iii) whose defect is not small (not run; benchmark n^alpha). DH, backward heat, E_a: outside the class (other gamma factor or no coefficient measure on [1, inf)); phase-rotated transfer operator, theta^w: not formulable "
